				"id": 2411382509,
				"number": 1152,
				"state": "open",
				"locked": false,
				"title": "Feat restricted controls",
				"body": "# Pull Request\r\n\r\n## Description\r\n\r\nThe goal of this PR was to implement some restricted access to certain controls for users who dont have the required role e.g. workspace settings. I used clerks built in protect component for the settings side bar so users can't view certain navigation links to workspace settings routes e.g. workspace members. Also if non admin users try to navigate to workspace settings routes via the URL the user is then redirected to the settings profile page so they can't view the route. Also this PR fixes a small issue with the getWorkspaceLabals api endpoint in which the wrong id is used. It has now been changed to check externalId.\r\n\r\nTicket [SQU-83](https://app-develop.squaredmade.com/squared/task/SQU-83/restricted-access-controls)\r\n\r\n## Type of change\r\n\r\n- [X] Bug fix (non-breaking change which fixes an issue)\r\n- [X] New feature (non-breaking change which adds functionality)\r\n- [ ] Refactoring (non-breaking change which refactors old code)\r\n- [ ] Design (Affects styling or design components)\r\n- [ ] Documentation (Improvements or additions to documentation)\r\n\r\n## How Has This Been Tested?\r\n\r\nPlease describe the tests that you ran to verify your changes. Provide instructions so we can reproduce.\r\n\r\nIf you have a member role in Squared check the settings nav bar component and check if you can view the workspace settings navigation links e.g. workspace labels and try to navigate to the route directly in the URL e.g. app/squared/settings/labels . Although if you are an admin you should be able to see the links and be able to navigate to the workspace settings routes.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\u003c!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai --\u003e\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n- **New Features**\n  - Introduced permission-based access control for workspace settings, labels, members, and GitHub integration management. UI elements and actions are now conditionally rendered or protected based on user permissions.\n  - Table columns and action buttons in settings pages dynamically adjust visibility and interactivity according to user permissions.\n\n- **Bug Fixes**\n  - Updated internal workspace label queries to align with permission and identification standards.\n\n- **Refactor**\n  - Replaced role-based UI restrictions with permission-based controls for more granular access management.\n  - Removed references to the deprecated \"org:owner\" role across components and types.\n\n- **Style**\n  - Minor formatting improvements for consistency.\n\n- **Chores**\n  - Updated global types to reflect current permission and role structures.\n\u003c!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai --\u003e\r\n\r\n[SQU-83]: https://app-develop.squaredmade.com/squared/task/SQU-83/restricted-access-controls\r\n\n\n\n\n\n\n",
